Falsifies `jh7110_entropy::verification::a_lockup_bit_is_never_overridden`.

The defect: `interpret` lets `RAND_RDY` outrank `LFSR_LOCKUP`, by taking the lockup arm only when
`RAND_RDY` is clear. The lockup latch is then ignored whenever a result is also standing, so bytes
from a core that reported a single-event upset are served as clean.

Expected to fail: the harness's `assert_eq!(interpret(stat, istat, rand), Outcome::Lockup)`: with both bits set (and
the core seeded) `interpret` returns `Ready`.

